  "summaryDescription": "Silver amulet holders, often containing symbolic material or a piece of paper with a magical or holy inscription, were worn throughout the Muslim world.  They were believed to protect the wearer from all kinds of physical and spiritual dangers.\r\n\r\nThis amulet case probably contains a tiny copy of the Koran.  It is dated AH 1240 (1825), and has a red cover, which can be seen through the glass opening on the front.  It may have been worn on the upper arm, fastened by straps which would have passed through the loops at either side. \r\n",
